replace(s(16,8),'This explains the theorem from Section',r'To finish the differentiation justification, let <m>P_N</m> be the polynomial partial sums and <m>G</m> the uniformly convergent sum of their derivatives on this smaller interval. The Fundamental Theorem gives <m>P_N(x)-P_N(a)=\int_a^x P_N\prime(t)\,dt</m>. Passing to the limit through the integral gives <m>F(x)-F(a)=\int_a^x G(t)\,dt</m>. Since <m>G</m> is continuous, another application of the Fundamental Theorem gives <m>F\prime=G</m>. This explains the theorem from Section','Uniform convergence of functions alone does not justify differentiating them')
